      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility shows χMT = 92.72 cm3 mol−1 K at 300 K, decreasing to 50.54 cm3 mol−1 K at 2 K, consistent with antiferromagnetic Gd···Gd interactions and/or ZFS. Magnetization at 2 K and 70 kOe is 85.85 Nβ. A magnetocaloric effect is observed with −ΔSm,max = 36.77 J kg−1 K−1 (63.76 mJ cm−3 K−1) at 2.0 K and ΔH = 70 kOe, below the 42.71 J kg−1 K−1 value calculated for 12 isolated Gd3+ ions.",
